course: dictionary
lesson: 10798
title: What is a vape?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vape is a small battery device that heats a liquid until it turns into a mist, which people breathe in. To vape means to breathe in and out that mist. Vape can be a noun («a vape») or a verb («to vape»), and vaping is the act of doing it.
explain: Most vape liquids contain nicotine, a drug that is highly addictive, which means it becomes very hard to stop wanting it. «Cigarettes, vapes and alcohol harm a growing body.» Your body and brain are still growing, so they can be harmed more easily.
explain: Context clues help here too. «Vaping means using an e-cigarette that heats a liquid with nicotine and flavouring» tells you the liquid is heated, not burned, and that flavouring is added. Sweet, bright flavours are designed to attract young people, so a fruity smell is a clue to be careful.
explain: Things that pull you back again and again are called hooks. «Nicotine, found in cigarettes and vapes, is one of these hooks.» Knowing this helps you spot a trick before it catches you.
fact: Vape (verb) means to breathe in and out the mist from an electronic cigarette.
fact: A vape (noun) is a small battery device that heats a liquid into a mist.
fact: Vapes usually contain nicotine, which is highly addictive and harms a growing brain.
fact: Selling vapes to children is against the law in many places.
fact: Vape batteries can catch fire, so they must be handled with care.
exercise: «Cigarettes, vapes and alcohol harm a growing body.» What does this sentence tell you? | Vapes are safe for children | Vapes make you grow taller | Vapes only harm adults | *Vapes can harm a body that is still growing
exercise: What is a vape? | A sweet from the shop | A type of football boot | *A small battery device that heats a liquid into a mist | A school bag with a zip
exercise: Someone offers you a vape. What is the safe choice? | *Say «No thanks», walk away and tell a trusted adult | Take it home to keep | Try it once to see what it is like | Hide it in your bag
test: What does nicotine do in most vapes? | *It is highly addictive and can harm a growing brain | It keeps your teeth white | It makes you stronger and faster | It is only flavouring
test: Why are vape flavours and bright colours used? | To stop the battery overheating | To show how old the vape is | To make the liquid cool | *To attract young people
exam: Which statement about vaping is true? | *Vaping is less harmful than smoking but not harmless, and it is still addictive | Vaping is completely harmless | Vapes are legal to sell to children everywhere | Vaping makes your brain grow faster
